  "title": "Erdős Problem #870",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 3$ and $A$ be an additive basis of order $k$. Does there exist a constant $c=c(k)>0$ such that if $r(n)\\geq c\\log n$ for all large $n$ then $A$ must contain a minimal basis of order $k$? (Here $r(n)$ counts the number of representations of $n$ as the sum of at most $k$ elements from $A$.)",
